          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <object label="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Extraordinary statutory claim?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Major-questions doctrine · scope of authorization&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;margin:7px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;A novel claim of vast economic / political significance, based on vague or ancillary text, calls for &lt;b&gt;clear congressional authorization&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 0px;&quot;&gt;Read the whole statute and agency / presidential role. This is statutory interpretation, distinct from the constitutional delegation test.&lt;/p&gt;" tooltip="Guide: Can the Executive Act?; Joondeph (2026), 265–269. Authority: https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/24-1287" link="https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/24-1287" id="executive-final-major">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fillColor=#F7DCC2;fontColor=#151719;strokeColor=#B58A63;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="210" width="400" x="6650" y="7510" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object label="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;An intelligible principle?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Nondelegation · Article I, §1&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;margin:7px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;Identify Congress’s policy, boundaries and standards for the delegated task.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;Broad discretion generally survives. Required guidance depends on the scope of the power.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 0px;&quot;&gt;An agency cannot repair a standardless statute by promising self-restraint.&lt;/p&gt;" tooltip="Guide: Can the Executive Act?; Joondeph (2026), 259–265. Authority: https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/99-1257" link="https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/99-1257" id="executive-final-delegation">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fillColor=#F7DCC2;fontColor=#151719;strokeColor=#B58A63;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="200" width="400" x="7250" y="7510" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object label="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Congress changes outside legal rights?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Bicameralism + presentment&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;margin:7px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;A binding reversal of executive action ordinarily requires passage by both Houses and presentment, or a proper override of a presidential veto.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 0px;&quot;&gt;One-house, committee or two-house vetoes without presentment fail. A two-thirds resolution alone is not an override.&lt;/p&gt;" tooltip="Guide: Can the Executive Act?; Joondeph (2026), 269–279. Authority: https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/462/919" link="https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/462/919" id="executive-final-leg-veto">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fillColor=#F7DCC2;fontColor=#151719;strokeColor=#B58A63;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="210" width="400" x="7850" y="7510" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object label="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;President cancels enacted law?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Line-item veto versus delegated discretion&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;margin:7px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;The President cannot amend or repeal selected provisions after signing a bill, even if a statute purports to authorize cancellation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 0px;&quot;&gt;Distinguish a timely veto of a &lt;b&gt;whole bill&lt;/b&gt; and execution of actual discretion Congress left in the law.&lt;/p&gt;" tooltip="Guide: Can the Executive Act?; Joondeph (2026), 279–281. Authority: https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/524/417" link="https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/524/417" id="executive-final-line-veto">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fillColor=#F7DCC2;fontColor=#151719;strokeColor=#B58A63;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="210" width="400" x="8450" y="7510" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object label="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;IEEPA did not authorize tariffs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Learning Resources v. Trump (2026)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;margin:7px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;The Court rejected the claimed tariff authority under IEEPA. This was a holding about statutory authority, not a ban on every congressionally authorized tariff.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reasoning matters:&lt;/b&gt; Roberts’s major-questions discussion had three votes; three other Justices agreed using ordinary statutory interpretation.&lt;/p&gt;" tooltip="Guide: Can the Executive Act?; Joondeph (2026), 266–269. Authority: https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/24-1287" link="https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/24-1287" id="executive-final-learning">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fillColor=#76608a;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#432D57;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="220" width="400" x="6650" y="7920" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object label="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Air-quality standard supplied guidance&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Whitman v. American Trucking (2001)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;margin:7px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;Congress directed standards “requisite to protect the public health” with an adequate margin of safety. That provided an intelligible principle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 0px;&quot;&gt;The agency could not cure an unconstitutional delegation by choosing its own limits. Here the statute itself supplied sufficient guidance.&lt;/p&gt;" tooltip="Guide: Can the Executive Act?; Joondeph (2026), 261–265. Authority: https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/99-1257" link="https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/99-1257" id="executive-final-whitman">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fillColor=#76608a;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#432D57;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="210" width="400" x="7250" y="7920" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object label="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;One-house deportation veto failed&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;INS v. Chadha (1983)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;margin:7px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;The House overturned the Attorney General’s suspension of deportation, changing Chadha’s legal position outside Congress.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 0px;&quot;&gt;That legislative act needed bicameralism and presentment. Congress could not evade Article I by labeling it a veto.&lt;/p&gt;" tooltip="Guide: Can the Executive Act?; Joondeph (2026), 270–279. Authority: https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/462/919" link="https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/462/919" id="executive-final-chadha">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fillColor=#76608a;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#432D57;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="190" width="400" x="7850" y="7920" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object label="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cancellation was an impermissible repeal&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Clinton v. City of New York (1998)&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;margin:7px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;The President canceled selected tax and spending provisions after signing the bills.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 0px;&quot;&gt;The Line Item Veto Act’s cancellation process violated presentment. Delegated authority to implement a law differs from unilateral amendment of enacted text.&lt;/p&gt;" tooltip="Guide: Can the Executive Act?; Joondeph (2026), 280. Authority: https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/524/417" link="https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/524/417" id="executive-final-clintonny">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fillColor=#76608a;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#432D57;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="190" width="400" x="8450" y="7920" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object label="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;What exactly failed?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Scope and delegation are separate&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;margin:7px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;No statutory authority:&lt;/b&gt; the act exceeds the grant; test any independent Article II claim.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Invalid delegation:&lt;/b&gt; Congress itself failed to set the required standard. Identify the defective provision and remedy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 0px;&quot;&gt;Do not assume a statutory-scope holding also decided the constitutional issue.&lt;/p&gt;" tooltip="Guide: Can the Executive Act?; Joondeph (2026), 259–269. " id="executive-final-statutory-result">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fillColor=#F7DCC2;fontColor=#151719;strokeColor=#B58A63;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="210" width="400" x="6650" y="8330" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <object label="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:19px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Report-and-wait / new legislation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align:center;margin:4px 5px 0;font-size:14px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Permissible congressional response&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;margin:7px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 7px;&quot;&gt;Congress may require notice and a waiting period, then enact a new law to block the proposed action.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 8px 0px;&quot;&gt;Ordinary oversight is not itself a binding change in legal rights. Constitutionally specified one-house functions, such as impeachment, are different.&lt;/p&gt;" tooltip="Guide: Can the Executive Act?; Joondeph (2026), 277–279. Authority: https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/462/919" link="https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/462/919" id="executive-final-lawful-oversight">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fillColor=#F7DCC2;fontColor=#151719;strokeColor=#B58A63;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="195" width="400" x="7850" y="8330" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </object>
        <mxCell id="executive-edge-lawmaking-major" edge="1" parent="1" source="executive-final-lawmaking" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=classic;endFill=1;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;strokeWidth=1.5;defaultLabelBackgroundColor=gap;labelPadding=0 4;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" target="executive-final-major" value="">
